# Obsidian vault (developer-io)

Persistent project memory lives in the Obsidian vault folder in this workspace:

`C:/Users/CLIET/.antigravity-ide/developer-io` (workspace root name: **developer-io (Obsidian)**)

## Cold start (mandatory)

1. Read **only** `Projects/CRMC-Aims/_Card.md` (or `Projects/CourtSync/_Card.md` for that project).
2. Open `Meta/Context-Loading-Protocol.md` and name any **additional** notes for this task **before** reading them.
3. Feature-scoped work → add **one** `Projects/<P>/Features/<slug>.md` — do **not** load full Architecture, Tasks, Sessions, or Components/Index unless the protocol says so.

## Do not

- Re-explore the repo when the card + feature note already name the hot paths
- Follow the old five-file bootstrap (Overview + Architecture + Conventions + Tasks + Sessions)
- Load `agents/*.examples.md` unless explicitly asked
- Use bare wikilinks like `[[Architecture]]` — use full paths under `Projects/CRMC-Aims/…`

## Session end

From vault root:

```bash
node Meta/scripts/vault-track.mjs session --project crmc-aims --write
node Meta/scripts/vault-track.mjs stale --project crmc-aims
```

Update `_Card.md` last-session / sprint line if it moved. Changelog only for pushed commits.

## Project overrides

When using specialized agents, also pass `Projects/CRMC-Aims/agent-overrides.md`.
